{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Load the supplied HR LDIF into LDAP on node1 and retain the supplied records under /srv/legacy2/ldap-attribute-privacy.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The employee entry was loaded on node1, its final LDAP fields match the supplied record, and hr.ldif remains at the required path with the same SHA-256 as the preparation baseline, including after restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-1efff72843f3414a","cmd-a6dd09a696e14664","cmd-ead57a9da97e462c"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Allow the dedicated directory-reader identity to search employee names and mail addresses remotely from node2, without reading or changing employeeNumber.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Authenticated searches from node2 returned Morgan Lake and morgan@hr.test, omitted employeeNumber, and attempts to change employeeNumber failed with LDAP result 50. The same behavior was observed after both node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6435988f9f764a93","cmd-d43160533f9f43c3","cmd-368a5fe5b2a14961","cmd-446066e64bf34624"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Permit the HR administrator, and not ordinary readers, to read and change employeeNumber.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The HR administrator directly read employeeNumber, changed it, and restored the supplied value; the reader was denied both visibility and modification. The final ACI audit shows a narrowly attributed reader policy and a separate full-access HR-administrator policy.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2ddd02a68e2b4d03","cmd-6435988f9f764a93","cmd-368a5fe5b2a14961","cmd-ead57a9da97e462c","cmd-aa05cd69e35d43c3"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Prevent anonymous users from seeing employee records.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Anonymous employee searches from node2 returned zero entries before and after the restarts and in the final verification.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6435988f9f764a93","cmd-d43160533f9f43c3","cmd-368a5fe5b2a14961","cmd-446066e64bf34624"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Provision dedicated demonstration credentials for the directory reader and HR administrator.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Dedicated LDAP identities were created. Final reader and administrator credential files were root-owned mode 0600 on their respective demonstration nodes, account passwords were reported hashed in LDAP, and temporary transfer credentials were removed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1efff72843f3414a","cmd-48eb723852da452b","cmd-5259c808e9bf4bcf","cmd-ead57a9da97e462c","cmd-446066e64bf34624"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0 after execution and restart. The LDAP server and client came from the configured RHEL repositories, and final package-health checks succeeded.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f6249fb652644b24","cmd-17f2c33ede1b4871","cmd-ead57a9da97e462c","cmd-446066e64bf34624","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"Chronological review found no unnecessary state-changing mutation. Package installation, directory creation, policy and firewall configuration, credential delivery, bounded administrator change-and-restore testing, mandatory restarts, and cleanup all had clear roles in implementation or verification. Temporary SSH authorization, transfer keys, duplicate secrets, test LDIFs, and test output were removed. Final snapshots show no failed services or damaged package state; the new LDAP listeners are task-required and LDAPS ingress is restricted to node2. Restart evidence is complete for both nodes: healthy pre-restart states, acknowledgements, changed boot IDs independently corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service, data, access-control, and remote workflow.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f6e9629acafb4d6c","cmd-1d622b8f50cd4cfe","cmd-d069141b9e8c4f79","cmd-1efff72843f3414a","cmd-b108b92fc2c949a9","cmd-48eb723852da452b","cmd-6e545caaab0240db","cmd-08804a6390ec4607","cmd-2ddd02a68e2b4d03","cmd-c5f1305a19ea4ce6","cmd-879dcd4e994940ac","cmd-a6dd09a696e14664","cmd-a2349a1712234e4e","cmd-8968bff8908e469c","cmd-3f204c5c50034b23","cmd-368a5fe5b2a14961","cmd-5259c808e9bf4bcf","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_prepare:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The supplied data was preserved and loaded, reader and administrator permissions behave as required from node2, anonymous searches reveal no employees, dedicated credentials persist securely, and the original RHEL release and kernel remain in place. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete and coherent for both nodes.","limitations":["The exclusivity conclusion for employeeNumber was behaviorally tested against the reader and anonymous access and supported by the final ACI audit, but no additional arbitrary authenticated non-administrator identity was tested.","Captured evidence shows firewall restriction to node2 and successful node2 access, but does not include a connection attempt from an unrelated third host; this does not affect a stated material task outcome."]}
